---
layout: changelog
title: "Create Firewall rules from ready-made presets"
date: 2026-09-21
cover: /images/blog/announcing-firewall-presets/cover.avif
tags: firewall, security, console
---

[Appwrite Firewall](/docs/products/firewall) now includes presets on the project API. Open **Firewall**, choose **Add preset**, and pick a policy for OTP abuse, country access, or scraping. Appwrite fills in the conditions and action, shows an impact preview, then creates ordinary rules you can edit, disable, or delete.

Nine presets ship today: rate-limit or geo-filter phone and email OTP, block or allow the API by country, rate-limit `/v1/` or `/v1/tablesdb`, and deny hosting or datacenter networks. The last two need the [premium Geo DB addon](/docs/products/firewall/conditions#premium-geo-db). Presets currently apply to API traffic, not to a single Function or Site.

If you keep recreating a rule that is not in the list, [open a GitHub issue](https://github.com/appwrite/appwrite/issues) with the policy you want next.

